The use of a double cast `(List<Attribute>) (List)` to convert the result of `visitQualifiedNamePatterns` is a workaround for Java's generic type erasure and produces compiler warnings (hence the `@SuppressWarnings("unchecked")`). A cleaner, more type-safe approach would be to map the elements of the list:
```java
List<Attribute> matchFields = visitQualifiedNamePatterns(ctx.qualifiedNamePatterns(), ne -> { 
    /* ... existing checks ... */ 
}).stream().map(ne -> (Attribute) ne).toList();
```

